2026-09-23T07:24:14.1064621Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1064841Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1064920Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065024Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065097Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065196Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065278Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065383Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065463Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065555Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065634Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065707Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065800Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065897Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1065971Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066047Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066138Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066215Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066434Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066601Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066695Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066768Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066863Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1066942Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067081Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067253Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067436Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067534Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067625Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067720Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067822Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1067895Z     
2026-09-23T07:24:14.1068009Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
